#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:3
msgid "Documentation development"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:5
msgid ""
"The documentation is a `Sphinx <https://www.sphinx-doc.org/>`_ site in "
"``docs/``, with sources in ``docs/source``. Three kinds of content live "
"there, and they are written differently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Prose** — the :doc:`whitepaper <../../overview/index>` and this "
"developer section. New prose is written in Markdown, with `MyST <https"
"://myst-parser.readthedocs.io/>`_ enabled, so a Sphinx directive is a "
"fenced block:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:21
msgid ""
"Older pages are reStructuredText and stay that way; there is no campaign "
"to convert them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:23
msgid ""
"**The Python API** — generated by ``autosummary`` from the installed "
"packages themselves, so it cannot drift. It really imports them, which is"
" why building the docs requires the extension module to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:27
msgid ""
"**The Rust API** — generated by ``cargo doc`` and published *beside* the "
"site under ``/rustdoc/``, not transcribed into ``.rst``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:31
msgid "Two rules that keep the side panel usable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:33
msgid ""
"The side panel is the **whole index of the site**: every page and every "
"section of every page is reachable from it, from anywhere, without having"
" to arrive at a page first to discover what is on it. Two things are "
"needed for that to keep working, and both are easy to break by accident."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:37
msgid ""
"**A section heading must make sense on its own.** In the panel it sits "
"between headings from forty other pages, with none of the surrounding "
"prose. ``The minimum``, ``Rules of this source`` and ``What it costs`` "
"were real headings here and told a reader nothing — the last one appeared"
" three times, on three different pages, meaning three different things. "
"Name the subject, not the rhetorical role: ``The four things a run "
"needs``, ``Rules of the command line``, ``What parallelism costs in "
"memory``. No two headings in the whitepaper should read identically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:44
msgid ""
"**A page's hidden toctree goes at the top of the page, above the first "
"section**, not at the bottom where it reads more naturally in the source."
" A directive belongs to whatever section encloses it, so a toctree at the"
" end of the file makes every child page a child of the *last section* — "
"which misstates the hierarchy and spends a level of ``navigation_depth`` "
"on nothing. The toctrees are ``:hidden:``, so moving them changes the "
"rendered page not at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:50
msgid ""
"``navigation_depth`` and ``collapse_navigation`` are set in ``conf.py`` "
"and carry a comment explaining the numbers; the depth has to cover the "
"deepest branch of the site *plus* its subsections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:55
msgid "Building"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:62
msgid ""
"``make docs-html`` skips regenerating rustdoc, which is what you want "
"while editing prose; ``make docs-rustdoc`` puts ``cargo doc`` output into"
" ``docs/source/_extra/rustdoc/``, from where Sphinx copies it into the "
"site verbatim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:68
msgid ""
"**Read the result with** ``make docs-serve``, **not by opening** "
"``docs/build/html/index.html``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:71
msgid ""
"Over a ``file://`` origin the search box does not work: it accepts a "
"query, says *Searching*, and stays there. Nothing is wrong with the build"
" — the index is complete — but ``searchtools.js`` fetches each result "
"page to build its excerpt, and a browser refuses a ``fetch`` from a file "
"origin. Rendering stops after the first result and the heading is never "
"updated, so the failure looks like a broken search rather than like a "
"blocked request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:77
msgid ""
"``make docs-serve`` puts the same directory behind "
"``http://localhost:8000`` and everything works. It is also what Read the "
"Docs does, which is why the published site has never shown the problem."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:81
msgid ""
"``make docs-site-coverage`` reports how much of the API **appears in the "
"built site**, which is not the same question as how much of it is "
"documented — it is a fact about how ``autosummary`` is configured. It was"
" called ``docs-coverage`` and was renamed for exactly that reason: every "
"module of the compiled ``freeports`` extension reports 100 % there "
"because ``inspect.getmembers`` attributes nothing to it. The figure that "
"is actually *gated* is docstring coverage, measured by ``make doc-"
"coverage-python``; :doc:`../devops/index` explains the difference and why"
" a threshold on the first one would be a threshold on a template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:89
msgid ""
"Building the site installs the three packages because autodoc imports "
"them for real — which is also why ``make dev-docs`` is not just the "
"Sphinx dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:92
msgid ""
"Read the Docs runs the same steps — its ``pre_build`` job is that same "
"``make -C docs rustdoc`` — so a build that works locally is a build that "
"publishes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:95
msgid "To build one language:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:101
msgid ""
"Generated output — ``docs/build/``, ``docs/source/_generated/`` and "
"``docs/source/_extra/`` — is ignored by git. It is produced by a build, "
"and a build product in version control goes stale the moment someone "
"forgets to regenerate it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/docs/building-the-site.rst:107
msgid ""
"The pages under ``validation/`` are **content-addressed**: their SHA-256 "
"hashes are recorded in signed validation documents, in this repository "
"and in others. Editing one — even fixing a typo — invalidates every grant"
" that cites it. Changing them is a deliberate operation that includes re-"
"granting and re-signing, not an act of tidying. See "
":doc:`../../overview/trust`."
msgstr ""

